        "title": "DeepGEMM",
        "summary": "DeepGEMM is a unified, high-performance tensor core kernel library that brings together the key computation primitives of modern large language models — GEMMs FP8, FP4, BF16, fused MoE with overlapped communication Mega MoE, MQA scoring for the lightning indexer, HyperConnection HC, and more — into a single, cohesive CUDA codebase. All kernels are compiled at runtime through DeepJIT, requiring no CUDA compilation during installation. DeepGEMM leverages some concepts from https://github.com/nvidia/cutlass and https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass/tree/main/include/cute, but avoids heavy reliance on their templates or algebras. The library is designed for simplicity, with only a limited number of ",
